  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the screen opened by the « Favoris » tab titled « Favoris » everywhere, as in the current app, so that the title matches the tab I tapped.\n\n### Observed (operator, iPhone, 2026-11-16)\n\nIn the bottom bar's « Favoris » tab, the title bar shows **« Drapeaux »**.\n\n### Cause (read from the code)\n\nThe tab shows the `.flagged` source, whose title is « Drapeaux » (`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicSource.swift:16`; `.favorites` is « Favoris », `:17`).\n\n### Legacy @ 87fe0d1c\n\nThe tab and its screen are « Favoris »: `HFRswift/Swift/MainWindow.swift:1821` (`.tabItem { Label(\"Favoris\", …) }`), `:2406` (`case .favorites: \"Favoris\"`), and `Favorites.swift:758` (`.navigationTitle(\"Favoris\")`), whatever the flag filter.\n\n### Wanted\n\n- The Favoris tab's screen is titled « Favoris », whatever the flag or filter shown (`.flagged`, `.favorites`, the #876 filters if they land), on iPhone, iPad and in a split.\n- Check every other place that shows « Drapeaux » as a title of that tab: back-button labels, the iPad sidebar, accessibility labels.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] « Favoris » as the title in the Favoris tab; a test on the title source fails without the change.\n- [ ] No « Drapeaux » title left for that tab.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
